                <pb facs="0440" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/3806: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-19T12:00:00-05:00">January 19,
                        1934—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Department’s 153, December 29, 3 p.m. and 5, January 15, 1934, 5 p.m. Please
                    seek an interview with the proper German authorities, especially Dr. Sehacht
                    and, if possible, the Chancellor himself, before the meeting of the bondholders
                    representatives on the 22nd, and supplementing such action as you may have taken
                    in accordance with the Department’s previous instructions, present the following
                    note:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of note identical with the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of January 19 to the German Embassy, printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>The President asks that you give this your immediate attention and advise us as
                    soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
